Z||000000||Standard||07-03-2001||03:02 PM||||I ordered a 1.2ghz T-bird from newegg.com a little bit ago.. been sitting around while I wait for the case.  Decided to take a closer look at it today and it looks like all the L1 bridges are closed!  I thought all Athlon's were multiplier locked?  Did I luck out or what?<P>Either way, I'll have some fun with this system..<BR>Abit KT7A Raid mobo<BR>1.2ghz Athlon T-bird<BR>256mb pc133 ram (for now)<BR>3d Prophet 4500<P>Gonna be a nice jump from the k6-2 350 I'm at now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/wacko.gif">  <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed (soon!!)<BR>1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<P>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus||||reg||5
Z||000001||LarryB||07-03-2001||03:59 PM||||Most T-birds ship from AMD unlocked.  <P>BTW, make sure you have a top-notch heatsink combo; Thunderbirds run hot by design and an inadequate fan/heatsink on the faster CPUs is a recipe for a smoked processor.  Best bet is to use one rated by AMD for 1.0GHz and faster processors.<P>What are the first 4 letters of the code? AVHA, AVIA, AXIA, BXHA, etc. etc. The batch # will give you some idea of how much fun you can have with it. <P>(My AVIA 1.2 GHz T-bird has been running @ 1.466GHz for the last couple of months. It'll post at 1.573GHz but is unstable during bootup.)<P>And yeah....you'll notice a bit of a difference over your K6-2 machine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>I ordered a 1.2ghz T-bird from newegg.com a little bit ago.. been sitting around while I wait for the case.  Decided to take a closer look at it today and it looks like all the L1 bridges are closed!  I thought all Athlon's were multiplier locked?  Did I luck out or what?<P>Either way, I'll have some fun with this system..<BR>Abit KT7A Raid mobo<BR>1.2ghz Athlon T-bird<BR>256mb pc133 ram (for now)<BR>3d Prophet 4500<P>Gonna be a nice jump from the k6-2 350 I'm at now   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||12
Z||000002||loafer87gt||07-03-2001||04:06 PM||||I found I got more luck increasing the bus speed on my 1.2Tbird than by increasing the multiplier. I am running 138 FSB and memory bus and it is rock solid at 1.3. I found that anything over that and Win98 was very unstable, but suprisingly enough Win2000 ran without a hitch. BTW, I just have to gloat that I picked up another 256 of ram now bringing my rig up to 1024 megs, MUWAHAHAHA!!! Gawd, and to think only about 6 or 7 years ago I paid just under a hundred dollars a meg for ram for my Amiga.<P>Edit: I just saw you got a Kyro II card, awesome, you'll have to let us know how the card performs. I've read a couple reviews and it sounds like the card is a real Darkhorse, and that in some tests it's even fast than a GeForce 2 ultra. If you have a moment, run the 3dmark 2001 default test and let me know how it scores.<p>[This message has been edited by loafer87gt (edited 07-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||07-03-2001||04:39 PM||||Oh, hell.  I thought you were trying to break into a car.  I thought my extensive criminal background might actually come in handy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||07-03-2001||11:50 PM||||I got the coolermaster h/s rated for 1.33 t-birds.  I'm not planning on doing any major o/cing till I get the whole system set up.<P>First 4 letters are AXIA, batch # 01158PLW<P>I can't wait to see what it scores in 3dmark.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||07-06-2001||12:26 PM||||Well, the bad news is that 3dMark isn't the best indicator of the Kyro II's ability.  The Kyro II has no hardware T&L and 3dMark 2001 is very dependent on hardware T&L.<P>So I only scored a pretty low 1953 in 3dmark 2001.  check out <A HREF="http://gamershq.madonion.com/products/orb/?3d2k1_details.shtml" TARGET=_blank>http://gamershq.madonion.com/products/orb/?3d2k1_details.shtml</A> <BR>Scored 5024 in 3dmark2000, running at 136Mhz bus speed, 4995 at 133mhz FSB. <A HREF="http://gamershq.madonion.com/products/orb/?publish_compare.shtml?&project_type=1&dprid=1863660" TARGET=_blank>http://gamershq.madonion.com/products/orb/?publish_compare.shtml?&project_type=1&dprid=1863660</A> <P>The coolest thing about this card is that it's hitting it's advertised fill rate!  NFS5 and Giants run flawlessy at full detail in 1024x768.  And looked daaaaaamn good.  Need to get more case fans and a good sound card now.  And start with the tweaking  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">     <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed (soon!!)  <BR>1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<P>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus||||reg||1
